{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "save-the-cat-oasis",
  "compatibility_date": "2025-11-01",
  "compatibility_flags": [
    "nodejs_compat"
  ],
  "main": ".open-next/worker.js",
  "assets": {
    "directory": ".open-next/assets",
    "binding": "ASSETS"
  },
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  },
  "routes": [
    {
      "pattern": "petition.oasishwc.qzz.io",
      "custom_domain": true
    }
  ],
  "vars": {
    "NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOWED_DOMAIN": "ccchwc.edu.hk",
    "NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID": "746639886925-mn51geoi7kprfoh7hcrm0rc7qroh3jtu.apps.googleusercontent.com",
    "BRAND": "oasis",
    "PETITION_TITLE": "Save the Cat",
    "PETITION_BODY": "Statement: Campus Cat Welfare and Demand for Public Accountability\n\nThe administration has announced its intent to remove two kittens from our campus under the guise of finding adopters. To this day, management has failed to provide a single transparent explanation regarding their care, vetting criteria, adopter background, or concrete timeline.\n\nWe have reason to question the administration's moral authority on this matter. It is widely understood within our school community that these kittens have been sustained, sheltered, and medically cared for through the personal dedication and financial contributions of students and frontline teachers, not executive management. We challenge the principal to disclose publicly what institutional resources, medical funding, or welfare support his office has ever provided for these animals.\n\nFurthermore, we categorically reject the claim that speaking behind closed doors with a select few teachers constitutes a “consultation”. Hand-picking a handful of staff members while systematically excluding the frontline caregivers, the student body, and elected student representatives is not dialogue. It is an administrative dictate dressed up as consensus.\n\nLet us be unequivocally clear: our clear priority is to explore every viable way to keep the kittens on campus, where students and teachers have already proven their commitment to caring for them. While we recognize that the animals' long-term wellbeing comes first, what we strongly oppose is treating immediate removal as the only option through an opaque, unilateral maneuver. Students are primary stakeholders in this community, not passive subjects to be silenced by top-down decrees.\n\nThe 52nd Students' Association Oasis hereby issues the following demands to school management:\n\n● Immediate suspension of any plan to remove the kittens until a fully public, representative dialogue takes place.\n\n● Full disclosure of the kittens' medical records, living conditions, daily care log, and financial sources to date.\n\n● A comprehensive, open exploration of feasible solutions to permanently house and care for the kittens on campus, establishing a clear student-led management framework rather than treating removal as the only option.\n\n● A direct, open, and equal dialogue between the principal, relevant frontline teachers, and the entire student body through the upcoming Students’ Forum.\n\n● A public accounting of the decision-making process, including who authorized this removal and the exact scope of consultation conducted.\n\nIf the administration persists in railroading this decision through administrative force while ignoring student voices, it will bear full responsibility for the irreversible breakdown of institutional trust, the complete failure of life education, and further public escalation.\n\nWe will not stand by while arbitrary authority overrides student consensus and animal welfare. The administration must face the student body directly.\n\n52nd Students’ Association Oasis\n\n——————————\n\n關於校園小貓去留及要求校方公開交代之聲明\n\n校方日前宣布，將為校園兩隻幼貓尋找領養者並送離學校。然而至今，校方未曾就現時照顧安排、審核準則或具體時間表，向全校師生作出任何公開透明的交代。\n\n我們有理由質疑校方在此事上的道德權威。眾所周知，兩隻幼貓一直只有前線老師親力親為照顧、收容及支付醫療費用，而非由管理層承擔。我們要求校長公開交代，校方曾為這兩隻幼貓提供過哪些制度性資源、醫療資助或福利支援。\n\n校方從未公開詢問老師和學生的意見。所謂「諮詢」並非對話，而是以共識包裝的行政命令。\n\n我們的明確立場，是優先探討所有讓幼貓留在校園的可行方案。我們深知，動物的長遠福祉永遠置於首位；但我們反對的，是校方未經充分探討校內照顧的可能性，便以單方面、不透明的方式，將立即送走視為唯一選項。學生是這個社群的主要持份者，並非任由自上而下命令擺布的被動對象。\n\n第52屆學生會 Oasis 在此向校方管理層提出以下要求：\n\n一、立即暫停任何送走幼貓的計劃，直至舉行全面公開、具代表性的對話。\n\n二、全面公開幼貓至今的醫療紀錄、生活環境、日常照顧紀錄及經費來源。\n\n三、全面公開探討在校園內長期安置及照顧幼貓的可行方案，並建立清晰的學生主導管理框架，而非將送走視為唯一選項。\n\n四、透過即將舉行的學生論壇（Students' Forum），由校長、相關前線老師及全體學生進行直接、公開、平等的對話。\n\n五、公開是次決定的決策過程，包括由誰授權送走幼貓，以及諮詢的實際範圍。\n\n倘若校方繼續以行政手段強行推進決定、無視學生聲音，校方須為制度信任的不可逆轉破裂、生命教育的徹底失敗，以及事態進一步公開升級，承擔全部責任。\n\n我們不會袖手旁觀，任由專斷權力凌駕學生共識與動物福利。校方必須直接面對全體學生。\n\n第52屆學生會 Oasis"
  }
}